      "text": "BSE Scrip Code : 536264 NSE Symbol : TIGERLOGS Registered office: D-174, GF, Okhla Industrial Area, Phase-1, New Delhi -110020 (India). Tel.: +91-11-47351111, Fax: +91-11-26229671; 26235205 Email: csvishal@tigerlogistics.in Website: www.tigerlogistics.in CIN: L74899DL2000PLC105817 13th August, 2026 To, BSE Ltd., P J Tower, Dalal Street, Mumbai 400001. To, National Stock Exchange of India Limited Exchange Plaza, Bandra-Kurla Complex, Bandra (E), Mumbai 400051 Sub: Disclosure under Regulation 30 of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015. Dear Sir, Pursuant to Regulation 30 of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015 and all the other applicable provisions thereto, please find attached Press Release along with the annexure, in compliance with SEBI Circular No. SEBI/HO/CFD/CFD-PoD-1/P/CIR/2023/123 dated July 13, 2023, and the subsequent circular dated November 11, 2024, and January 30, 2026. Kindly take on record the above. Thanking You For Tiger Logistics (India) Limited Vishal Saurav Company Secretary & Compliance Officer VISHAL SAURAV Digitally signed by VISHAL SAURAV Date: 2026.08.13 20:30:33 +05'30' Tiger LogisƟcs to Execute 310 MT Project Cargo in Three Air Charter Flights for HPCL Tiger LogisƟcs (India) Ltd., a leading end-to-end internaƟonal logisƟcs soluƟons provider, has secured two major air import contracts from Hindustan Petroleum CorporaƟon Limited (HPCL) for the transportaƟon of approximately 310 MT of cargo, to Visakhapatnam. The contracts, represenƟng a business value of approximately ₹8.8 crore, will be executed through three chartered ﬂights, with approximately 80 MT being transported from France and 210 MT from Saudi Arabia. Under the contracts, Tiger LogisƟcs will manage the shipments on an end-to-end ex-works basis, covering the complete logisƟcs chain from origin to desƟnaƟon. The scope includes air freight, customs clearance and local transportaƟon, ensuring seamless handling and delivery of the specialized cargo from the origins in both countries to the designated desƟnaƟon in Visakhapatnam, India. The scale and nature of the assignment underline Tiger LogisƟcs' growing capabiliƟes in handling Ɵme-sensiƟve and specialized air cargo movements for large public sector undertakings. The contracts further strengthen Tiger LogisƟcs' growing experƟse in air imports for PSUs, building on its experience of execuƟng specialized logisƟcs assignments for leading public sector enterprises, including Bharat Heavy Electricals Limited (BHEL). The renewed trust placed by HPCL reﬂects the company's ability to manage complex, high-value and specialized cargo movements with operaƟonal precision. Key Highlights  310 MT of specialized project cargo to be transported in Three chartered ﬂights planned for seamless movement of the cargo.  Project includes 80 MT from France and 210 MT from Saudi Arabia to Visakhapatnam, India.  End-to-end logisƟcs scope covering air freight, customs clearance and local transportaƟon from origin in France and Saudi Arabia to Visakhapatnam, India.  Strengthens Tiger LogisƟcs’ air cargo handling capabiliƟes for PSUs, building on experience with BHEL and renewed trust from HPCL. CommenƟng on the development, Harpreet Singh Malhotra, Chairman & Managing Director, Tiger LogisƟcs (India) Ltd., said, “Securing these two contracts from HPCL is a strong endorsement of our capabiliƟes in handling complex air cargo project movements using chartered aircraŌs. Such handling requires stringent planning, regulatory compliance and seamless coordinaƟon across mulƟple touchpoints. Our ability to provide an end-to-end logisƟcs soluƟon allows us to manage such assignments with greater control and reliability. We are conﬁdent that our growing experience with PSUs will enable us to deepen these relaƟonships and undertake larger and more specialised logisƟcs projects in the future.” ……………………………………………………………………………………………………………………………………………………. Annexure - I Disclosure under SEBI Circular No. SEBI/HO/CFD/CFD-PoD-1/P/CIR/2023/123 dated July 13, 2023, and the subsequent circular dated November 11, 2024, and January 30, 2026. Sr. No. Particulars Tiger Logistics Comments 1 Name of the entity awarding the order(s)/contract(s) Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Limited (HPCL) 2 significant terms and conditions of order(s)/contract(s) awarded in brief Tiger Logistics will handle air freight, customs clearance and inland transportation operations. 3 whether order(s) / contract(s) have been awarded by domestic/ international entity; Domestic entity 4 nature of order(s) / contract(s); Air Freight, Customs clearance and inland transportation operations. 5 whether domestic or international International 6 time period by which the order(s)/contract(s) is to be executed One Year 7 broad consideration or size of the order(s)/contract(s); Rs. 8.80 Crores (approx.) 8 whether the promoter/ promoter group / group companies have any interest in the entity that awarded the order(s)/contract(s)? If yes, nature of interest and details thereof No 9 whether the order(s)/contract(s) would fall within related party transactions? If yes, whether the same is done at “arm’s length”. No",
