      "text": "INVESTOR PRESENTATION Q1 FY27 Powering the N ext P hase of G rowth Safe Harbour Statement This presentation is not intended to, and does not, constitute or form part of any offer, invitation or solicitation of an offer to purchase, acquire, subscribe for, sell or otherwise deal in any securities of Paramount Communications Limited (\"Paramount\" or \"the Company\"), nor shall it or the fact of its distribution form the basis of, or be relied upon in connection with, any contract or investment decision . Certain figures and information in this presentation are indicative and provisional in nature and may be subject to change . Estimates and projections relating to the economy, the wires and cables industry, the Company and related areas are based on current assumptions and are inherently subject to change due to market conditions and a variety of other factors beyond the Company's control . This presentation contains certain forward - looking statements concerning the Company's future business prospects and business profitability, which are subject to a number of risks and uncertainties, and the actual results could materially differ from those in such forward - looking statements . The risks and uncertainties relating to these statements include, but are not limited to, risks and uncertainties regarding fluctuations in earnings, fluctuations in the prices of key raw materials, our ability to manage growth and successfully implement our expansion plans, competition (both domestic and international), economic growth in India and abroad, changes in government policies, trade and tariff regulations, our ability to attract and retain highly skilled professionals, time and cost overruns on projects, currency exchange rate fluctuations, our ability to manage our international operations, and interest rates and other fiscal costs generally prevailing in the economy . The Company does not undertake to make any announcement in case any of these forward - looking statements become materially incorrect in future or update any forward - looking statements made from time to time by or on behalf of the Company . We have started FY 27 on a strong note, with healthy growth across both revenue and profitability compared with the corresponding period last year . The performance reflects sustained demand across our key business segments, coupled with improved operating efficiencies and disciplined executions . We continue to see encouraging opportunities across the power sector, especially transmission & distribution, data centers, renewables and infrastructure sectors, while our specialized cable portfolio and international business provide additional avenues for growth . Our focus remains on strengthening our product capabilities and expanding our presence across domestic and international markets . With a healthy business pipeline and supportive underlying demand, we remain confident about maintaining this momentum through the year and creating sustainable, long - term value for our stakeholders . Management Commentary SANJAY AGGARWAL Chairman & CEO “ “ Table of Contents PARAMOUNT AT A GLANCE • Company Snapshot • Our Value Chain • Journey • Why Paramount 01 WIRE & CABLES SECTOR AT A GLANCE • Industry Opportunity 02 OPERATING SCALE • Product Portfolio • Manufacturing & Capacity • Geographic Presence • Revenue Mix • Export Flexibility • Order Book 03 FINANCIAL PERFORMANCE • Revenue Trajectory • Q1 FY27 Quarterly Update • Income Statement • Balance Sheet 04 FY27 OUTLOOK • FY27 Roadmap that Defines the Next Phase of Growth 05 ANNEXURES • Key Management Team • Certifications & Marquee Clientele • ESG • Shareholding Pattern 06 Paramount at a Glance 01 A Platform built for the next Infrastructure Cycle ₹ 583 Cr Order book 31 Mar 2026 29,664 Metal throughput MTPA | FY26 35+ Presence across E xport G eographies 8 US distributors 35.4% 4 - Year Revenue CAGR 48.5% 4 - Year EBITDA CAGR 64.6% 4 - Year PAT CAGR 2 (+1) Manufacturing Plants (3rd under construction) Largest Indian LV Cable Exporter to the U.S. in CY2025 950+ Institutional C lients Our Value Chain Copper & Aluminum from domestic vendors Sourcing raw materials Product Development & Innovation Research 2 production facilities in Rajasthan & Haryana Manufacturing process Copper/ Aluminum wire Dispatch Bunching/ Stranding Core insulation Outer sheathing of cables Final testing/High Voltage Test etc Laying of cores Taping & braiding of co - axial/shielding cables End - To - End Capabilities Strategic Sourcing Integrated Manufacturing Quality & Testing Distribution Network End Markets Served • Quality raw materials • Long term supplier relationships • Stringent incoming quality checks • Automated & technology - driven production line • Greenfield EHV facility under construction (Narmadapuram, M.P) • In house testing at every stage of production • High voltage & routine testing • Global certification UL, BIS, ROSO, ISO • 950+ Institutional Clients • 250+ Channel Partners • Pan - India distribution presence • 35+ Export Geographies • Power Transmission & Distribution • Railway & Metro • Telecom • Renewable Energy • Industrial, Defense, EPC Projects • Data Centers Input Manufacturing Process Market Seven Decades of Capability Building 1955 Established Paramount; built a trusted brand in house wires & cables. 1976 1985 1996 1999 2017 2019 2020 2023 2026 Launched PVC Telecom Cables for the Department of Telecommunications. Pioneered Axle Counter Cables for Indian Railways. Commissioned PIJF Cable manufacturing facility at Dharuhera. Commissioned Optical Fibre Cable manufacturing facility. 2016 Entered Solar Cables, strengthening renewable energy portfolio. 2012 Entered Fire Survival Cables with BASEC & LPCB approvals. 2008 Launched India's first Lead - Free House Wires. 2005 Expanded into HT & LT Power Cables. Expanded into EPC & Turnkey Project Solutions. Executed Submarine Cable Repair Project. Accelerated focus on export markets. Exports contributed ~50% of revenue. Crossed ₹ 1,900 Cr revenue; acquired Narmadapuram land for Greenfield EHV expansion.",
