      "text": "Registered Office: L&T House, N. M. Marg, Ballard Estate, Mumbai - 400 001. INDIA CIN: L72900MH2012PLC232169 Tel: +91 22 6892 5257 Fax: +91 2267525858 L&T Technology Services is a subsidiary of Larsen & Toubro Limited L&T Technology Services Limited A.M. Naik Tower,6th Floor, L&T Campus, Gate No.3, Jogeshwari-Vikhroli Link Road, Powai, Mumbai-400072. www.ltts.com August 17, 2026 National Stock Exchange of India Limited Exchange Plaza, C-1, Block G, Bandra-Kurla Complex Bandra (East), Mumbai – 400 051 NSE Symbol: LTTS BSE Limited Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai400 001 BSE Scrip Code: 540115 Dear Sir/Madam, Subject: Disclosure pursuant to Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 – Presentation of Analyst Meet Pursuant to Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations & Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, and in continuation to our letter dated August 12, 2026, please find enclosed the copy of the presentation to be made to the analyst(s) / investor(s) during the “Non-Deal Roadshow ” scheduled to be held from August 18, 2026, till August 21, 2026 at Singapore and Hong Kong. The said presentation is also being uploaded on the website of the Company at www.ltts.com. Kindly take the above information on record. Thanking You, Yours sincerely, For L&T Technology Services Limited Prasad Shanbhag Company Secretary & Compliance Officer (M. No. A 30254) Encl.: As above 1www.LTTS.com INVESTOR PRESENTATION August 2026 2www.LTTS.com ER&D: Growth Drivers and Emerging Themes LTTS: Pivot on Growth Powered by Engineering Intelligence (EI) From Better to Best 01. 03. 04. 02. 3www.LTTS.com World Today – Broad Macro Themes Global GDP Growth Revised down from 3.3% — Middle East conflict and trade fragmentation3.1 % Global IT Spend Up 13.5% YoY — AI infra emerging as the core growth driver$6.31 T Fiscal Pressures & Monetary Policy Macro pressures (high debt, rates) accelerating shift to outcomebased, risk-sharing models AI as Economic Engine AI scaling from pilots to enterprise-wide industrial adoption Reindustrialization & Supply Chain Reshoring & friendshoring accelerating reindustrialization— India well placed to benefit Energy Transition & Data Centers Power availability emerging as a key constraint amid rising AI demand Engineering spend is decoupling from GDP — Outcome ownership will determine who captures market share 4www.LTTS.com AI is reshaping the tech landscape—fast, wide, and power-hungry ADVANCING AI ER&D: TRANSLATES TO ENGG DOLLARS • 59% of companies using Gen AI in ER&D for augmenting product features and personalization according to Nasscom • $380B Capex by 4 hyperscalers (Silicon design, AI application, Models & Services). ENERGY INFRASTRUCTURE CRITICALITY • Datacenter power demand to reach ~92 GW by 2027. • Grid and permitting delays causing bottlenecks. AI SOFTWARE LANDSCAPE • AI application software surging to $270B+ in 2026 • Rapid scaling: 64% of enterprises now actively use AI HYPERSCALER AI & COMPUTE BUILDOUT • Datacenter capex to reach $6.7T by 2030; $5.2T for AI. • AI Capex to exceed $500B by 2026; upside to $700B.. Sources: Goldman Sachs Research, McKinsey, J.P. Morgan Outlook 2026, ComSoc, Gartner, Kotak Securities, NVIDIA blog 5www.LTTS.com 55% 65% 39% 61% 75% 78% 49% 67% 32% 53% 20% 42% 67% 73% 40% 48% 2023 2030 ER&D is Entering a New Growth Cycle Spend pools are expanding and digital intensity is rising in every sector 2023E 2030F 86 156 68 116 76 157 136 219 157 280 153 290 553 900 293 536 384 616 ER&D spend by sector ($B) Digital engineering share of sector R&D spend: 2023 to 2030 Shift CAGR Healthcare & Medtech 6-7% Automotive 8-9% Software & Consumer El. 7-8% Semiconductor 9-10% Manufacturing & Constr. 8-9% Energy, Oil & Gas, Util. 7-8% Telecommunications 10-11% Aerospace & Defence 7-8% Overall digital engineering mix 45% → 65% +20bps What it Means $1.4-1.8T $2.5-3.3T Others considered as 5% of total; % here indicates sector's share of global business ER&D spend CAGR 8-9% Traditional sectors such as automotive and software remain the anchor of ER&D spend Healthcare/medtech, SW & Cons., manufacturing and E&U are key hotspots for ER&D spending Digital intensity rapidly increasing across sectors, with higher impact in HC/medtech, semicon and telecom ER&D sourcing market to double by 2030 ($750-800B) High degree of investment in cybersecurity, predictive analytics, IoT & cloud connectivity Cost dynamics and access to new-age, digitalready talent drive sourcing decisions 6www.LTTS.com Segment What the market is signalling What it means for LTTS How LTTS is positioned S&P Intelliswift AI is compressing effort-based work — value is shifting decisively from staffing to IP, platforms and outcome-based engagements Moving up the value curve — leading with solutions, marketplaces and PE-led selling, anchored on our Engineering Intelligence platform Big Bet: Software Platforms & EI MedTech Devices · Pharma Healthcare/Medtech 6–7% CAGR and a named hotspot; digital engineering share rising 55% → 65%. Driven by Robotic surgery, precision & connected health platforms Repositioning for the digital-health shift — broadening beyond legacy accounts and deepening Pharma to build predictable lifecycle revenue Big Bet: MedTech (+ targeted M&A) Positioning: LEADING /SCALING = growth engines TRANSFORMING = moving up the value curve EXPANDING = scaling into a growth pool Mobility Auto · Aero & Rail . T&OH Auto R&D 8–9% CAGR; digital engineering share leaping 39% → 61% — the sharpest of any sector. SDV, EV/hybrid & autonomy to lead Growth accelerating — led by Aerospace and North America, with electrification/hybrid and software-defined programs broadening the base Big Bet: Software-Defined Mobility Sustainability Plant Engineering Industrial Products Energy demand to double by 2050; LNG expansion, reindustrialization & data-centre buildout driving sustained engineering capex Our flagship engine — active wins across O&G, HVAC companies, amplified by AI-led information management Big Bets: Plant Buildout + Digital Mfg. M&T Comms · Media · Tech Highest-growth pools — Semiconductor & Telecom in double digits. AI-infrastructure and silicon capex are the structural tailwind Building Momentum: Semiconductor engineering, Telecom infrastructure supported by large deal wins Big Bet: Next-Gen Compute & AI Infra ER&D Current Market View SCALING Near Term Challenge: soft Europe LEADING Near Term Challenges: Decision delays SCALING EXPANDING TRANSFORMING Near Term Challenges: Contingent on deal conversion & margin discipline Near Term Challenges: Pivoting to AI Near Term Challenges: Repositioning to MedTech & Pharma Engineering story 7www.LTTS.com LTTS’ TAM Poised for Growth LTTS Segments Business process Expanded Total Addressable Market (TAM) Mobility Plant Engg. Industrial MedTech M&T S&P New Product Development Product Sustenance Customer support Supply chain Manufacturing Data Centre Infrastructure & Components Data Engineering & AI Platform partnerships Data Centre Buildout & Modernisation Silicon Engineering Full Rack Integration $57B $207B $230B $57B $150B Physical AI AI Tool Chain AI in Devices AI on Edge (Sima.ai) Industrial Automation $55B LightSpeed AI",
