      "text": "बडौदा कॉपȾरेट सɅटर, सी-26, जी-Þ लॉक, बाÛġा कुला[ कॉà Ü लेÈ स, मुंबई 400 051, भारत. Baroda Corporate Centre, Bandra Kurla Complex, Mumbai 400 051, India फोन / Ph : 91 22 6698 5812 ई मेल / E Mail : companysecretary.bcc@bankofbaroda.bank.in वेब / Web : www.bankofbaroda.bank.in BCC:ISD:118:16:429 17.08.2026 The Vice-President, B S E Ltd. Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers Dalal Street Mumbai – 400 001 BSE CODE-532134 The Vice-President, National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. Exchange Plaza, Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra (E) Mumbai – 400 051 CODE-BANKBARODA Madam/Dear Sir, Re: Bank of Baroda – Rating We advise Ratings from various Rating Agency in connection with the issuances of US$ notes under MTN programme as under: SR No. ISIN No. Rating Agency Ratings 1 XS3424472010 Fitch Ratings BBB2 XS3424472101 Fitch Ratings BBB3 XS3424472010 S&P Global Rating BBB 4 XS3424472101 S&P Global Rating BBB 5 XS3424472010 CareEdge Global BBB+/Stable 6 XS3424472101 CareEdge Global BBB+/Stable The detailed report is enclosed. We request you to take note of the above pursuant to Regulation 30 of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015 and disseminate the information on your website. Yours faithfully, S Balakumar Company Secretary FitchRatin s August 17, 2026 Mr. Nishant Ranjan Chief General Manager & Head, International Banking Division Bank of Baroda Baroda Corporate Center C 26 G Block Sandra Kurla Complex Mumbai, 400051 lndja Dear Mr. Ranjan: Re: Fitch rating assignment regarding Bank of Baroda Fitch (see definition below) assigns the following ratings. Bank of Baroda Debt Issue Rating Rating Previous Rating Action · Identifiers ~ I Rating senior unsecured USD 300 min LT B~BNew Rating XS3424472010 5.318% bond/note I (ISIN) 20-Aug-2031 senior unsecured ,USD300 min LT (xgs) BB(xgs) New Rating XS3424472010 5.318% bond/note I (ISIN) 20-Aug-2031 senior unsecured USD400 min LT BBBBBB-(EXP) New Rating XS3424472101 5.114% bond/note (ISIN) 20-Aug-2029 senior unsecured USO 400 min LT (xgs) BB(xgs) BB(xgs)(EXP) New Rating XS3424472101 5.114% bond/note (ISIN) 20-Aug-2029 RATINGS KEY OUTLOOK WATCH Positive Negative Page 1 of 4 Fitch F'.s:inp Ltd, 3D North '+\"\"''\"\"\"\"\" CID1&1:y\"\\Vhar.i. Lor1<CLn1El-+ 5G:,J T +44 2-0 3:3-0 !vOD I?itchRatings Evolving ♦ Stable 0 The final rating will be published on Fitch's public website under https://www.fitchratings.com/entity/bank-of-baroda-80360486 Fitch Ratings has assigned Bank of Baroda's (BOB, BBB-/Stabie) USD400 million 5.114% senior unsecured notes due August 2029 and USD300 million 5.318% senior unsecured notes due August 2031 final ratings of 'BBB-'. This follows the completion of the securities issue and the receipt of final documents conforming to information previously received. The final ratings are the same as the expected rating assigned on 21 June 2026. The securities constitute BOB's direct, unconditional, unsubordinated and unsecured obligations and will at all times rank pari passu among themselves and with all of BOB's other unsubordinated and unsecured obligations. The notes were issued by BOB's Gujarat International Finance Tee-City Branch. Key Rating Drivers The senior unsecured instruments are rated at the same level as the bank's Long-Term Issuer Default Rating (IDR), in line with Fitch's criteria. BO B's IDR is driven by its Government Support Rating (GSR) of 'bbb-', which reflects our view of a high probability of extraordinary state support for the bank, if required. This takes into consideration the state's 64% ownership, BOB's position as India's second-largest state bank and our assessment that the state has a strong propensity to support the banking system in general. The Stable Outlook on the IDR mirrors that on the sovereign IDR (BBB-/Stable). For mere details on BOB's ratings and credit profile, see Fitch Affirms Bank of Baroda and Bank of Baroda New Zealand at 'BBB-; Upgrades VR to 'bb', published 25 February 2026. Rating Sensitivities Factors that could, individually or collectively, lead to positive rating action/upgrade The ratings of BOB's senior unsecured notes are broadly sensitive to the same considerations that aff ect its IDR and Long-Term IDR (xgs). A positive rating action on the IDR or Long-Term IDR (xgs) would result in a similar change in the ratings of the notes. Factors that could, individually or collectively, lead to negative rating action/downgradP. A negative change in the !DR or Long-Term !DR (xgs) would result in a similar change in the ratings of BOB's senior unsecured notes. Disclaimer and Limitations In issuing and maintaining its ratings, Fitch relies on factual information it receives from issuers and underwriters and from other sources Fitch believes to be credible. Fitch conducts a reasonable investigation of the factual information relied· upon by it in accordance with its ratings methodology·, and obtains reasonable verification of that information from independent sources, to the extent such sources are available for a given security or issuer or obligor in a given jurisdiction. Page 2 of 4 Fitch F~i;.tings Ltd, 3{i Nor'\"J1Cr..\"l.cinnaci~-: ·Ca..'\"1.:1 •• ry VVhar.( London El4 SGN 1 ...-44 2:(i J530 !-000 F_--44 10 35l-{i 1000 -vr,,,-,;·.:fl.tcht\"a.tin.E:LCO.n1 R2·gist;re6. !1\".: EriiLmd ·s:r11.:. \\Vai.zs No. 111623D FitchRatings The manner of Fitch's factual investigation and the scope of the third-party verification it obtains will vary depending on the nature of the rated security and its issuer, the requirements and practices in the jurisdiction in which the rated security is offered and sold and/or the issuer is located, the availability and nature of relevant public information, access to the management of the issuer and its advisers, the availability of pre-existing third-party verifications such as audit reports, agreed-upon procedures letters, appraisals, actuarial reports, engineering reports, legal opinions and other reports provided by third parties, the availability of independent and competent thir