      "text": "J. G. Chemicals Limited (An ISO 9001, 14001, 45001 CERTIFIED COMPANY) Adventz Inﬁnity@5, Unit No. 1511, Street No. 18, BN Block, Sector – V, Salt Lake City, Kolkata – 700 091, India, Phone: +91 33 4415 0100 Email: cs@jgchem.com | Web: www.jgchem.com Mfg. of : “LUXMI” BRAND ZINC OXIDE(UR) CIN: L24100WB2001PLC093380 18th August, 2026 To, To, Listing Department, Department of Corporate Services, National Stock Exchange of India Ltd, BSE Ltd., Exchange Plaza, 5th Floor P.J. Towers, Plot No. - C/1, “G” Block, Dalal Street, Fort, Bandra – Kurla Complex, Bandra (E), Mumbai – 400001 Mumbai – 400051 BSE Code – 544138 NSE Code – JGCHEM ISIN: INE0MB501011 ISIN: INE0MB501011 Dear Sir/Madam, Sub: Intimation of Material EventAcquisition of Land Ref: Announcement under Regulation 30(3) & 30(9) of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015. Pursuant to Regulation 30(3) & 30(9) of Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, we are pleased to inform you that BDJ Oxides Private Limited, our Material Subsidiary Company has acquired a freehold land admeasuring approximately 16.74 acres situated at APIIC Industrial Park, Village – Attivaram, Mondal – Ozili; District – Tirupati, Andhra Pradesh – 524421, demarked as Plot No. 9/2, for its future expansion and development of its sustainable recycling product portfolio. The total consideration for the acquisition is Rs. 18.41 Crores, in addition to applicable registration charges and other charges/levies Kindly take this information on record. Yours faithfully, For J.G.Chemicals Limited Swati Poddar Company Secretary and Compliance Officer J. G. Chemicals Limited (An ISO 9001, 14001, 45001 CERTIFIED COMPANY) Adventz Inﬁnity@5, Unit No. 1511, Street No. 18, BN Block, Sector – V, Salt Lake City, Kolkata – 700 091, India, Phone: +91 33 4415 0100 Email: cs@jgchem.com | Web: www.jgchem.com Mfg. of : “LUXMI” BRAND ZINC OXIDE(UR) CIN: L24100WB2001PLC093380 Press Release J.G.Chemicals Strengthens Long-Term Expansion Platform as Material Subsidiary-BDJ Oxides Acquires 16.74 Acres in Andhra Pradesh Kolkata, August 18, 2026: JG Chemicals Limited, India’s largest Zinc Oxide (ZnO) manufacturer and one of the leading zinc recycling companies globally, today announced that its Material Subsidiary, BDJ Oxides Private Limited, has acquired approximately 16.74 acres of freehold land at APIIC Industrial Park, Attivaram, Tirupati, Andhra Pradesh. The acquisition is part of the Company’s long-term strategy to expand its sustainable recycling and zinc-based product portfolio and strengthen its manufacturing footprint. Strategic Location to Support Future Expansion The newly acquired land is located directly opposite BDJ Oxides’ existing manufacturing facility at Naidupeta, Andhra Pradesh, creating a strategically advantageous opportunity for future expansion. The acquisition, with a total consideration of Rs. 18.41 crore, plus applicable registration charges and other charges/levies, provides JG Chemicals with a ready platform for its future growth plans. The Company intends to utilise the land for expansion of its sustainable recycling product portfolio and potentially develop additional manufacturing capabilities as opportunities emerge. Commenting on the development, Mr. Anirudh Jhunjhunwala – Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer of JG Chemicals Limited said, “This acquisition represents an important step in our long-term expansion journey. The strategic piece of land is located right opposite our existing Naidupeta manufacturing facility, providing us with an opportunity to leverage our existing infrastructure and capabilities as we expand in the future. We believe this investment will provide us with the flexibility to pursue future growth opportunities while strengthening our manufacturing ecosystem in Andhra Pradesh.” J. G. Chemicals Limited (An ISO 9001, 14001, 45001 CERTIFIED COMPANY) Adventz Inﬁnity@5, Unit No. 1511, Street No. 18, BN Block, Sector – V, Salt Lake City, Kolkata – 700 091, India, Phone: +91 33 4415 0100 Email: cs@jgchem.com | Web: www.jgchem.com Mfg. of : “LUXMI” BRAND ZINC OXIDE(UR) CIN: L24100WB2001PLC093380 About JG Chemicals Limited JG Chemicals Limited (JGCL), incorporated in 1975, is India’s largest manufacturer of Zinc Oxide and among the top five global manufacturers, with a total zinc chemicals capacity of 70,000 MTPA. The Company is also India’s largest zinc recycling company, with strong inhouse recycling technology for processing various forms of zinc waste and scrap. JGCL serves 200+ domestic and 50+ global customers across more than 10 countries, catering to diverse industries including Rubber & Tyres, Pharmaceuticals, Ceramics, Paints & Coatings, Agriculture, Electronics, Batteries and Specialty Chemicals. With more than five decades of manufacturing experience, JGCL has built strong customer relationships, technical expertise and manufacturing capabilities, serving 9 of the top 10 global tyre manufacturers. The Company is steadily diversifying into higher-value applications and strengthening its sustainable portfolio through R&D, recycling and green manufacturing initiatives. Its recycled-zinc-led business model supports a circular economy. Disclaimer Certain statements that are made may be forward-looking statements. Such forward-looking statements are subject to certain risks and uncertainties, such as significant changes in the economic environment in India and abroad. Actual results might differ substantially from those expressed or implied. The Company shall not be in any way responsible for any action taken based on such statements and discussions. The Company also undertakes no obligation to publicly update these forward-looking statements to reflect subsequent events or circumstances. Contact Information Investor Relations – Go India Advisors Ms. Sana Kapoor - sana@GoIndiaAdvisors.com - 81465 50469 Ms. Sakshi Narvekar - SakshiN@GoIndiaAdvisors.com - 87792 63625 JG Chemicals Limited Swati Poddar (Company Secretary) - cs@jgchem.com",
