arred from holding the office by virtue of any SEBI Order or any other authority. Other information as per SEBI Master Circular dt. 30th January, 2026 is enclosed at Annexure-A. The above is being informed in terms of Regulation 30 of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, as amended. The Board Meeting commenced at 3:05 P.M. (IST) and concluded at 3:15 P.M. (IST). Thanking You. Yours faithfully, (Anjana Luthra) Company Secretary & Compliance Officer Encl.: As above क े न्द्रीय कायाालय: \"सौदामिनी\", प्लॉट नंबर 2, सेक्टर -29, गुरुग्राि -122001, (हररयाणा) द ू रभाष: 0124-2822999 & 2822000 Corporate Office: “Saudamini”, Plot No. 2, Sector-29, Gurugram-122001, (Haryana) Tel.: 0124-2822999 & 2822000 पंजीक ृ त कायाालय: बी -9, क ु तुब इंस्टीट्यूशनल एररया, कटवाररया सराय, नई मदल्ली -110 016. द ू रभाष: 011-26560112, 26560115 & 26560193, CIN: L40101DL1989GOI038121 Registered Office: B-9, Qutab Institutional Area, Katwaria Sarai, New Delhi -110 016. Tel: 011-26560112, 26560115 & 26560193, CIN : L40101DL1989GOI038121 Website: www.powergrid.in Annexure-A Name Shri Amol Babulal Taori (DIN:11890590) Reason for change Appointment Date of Appointment and Term of Appointment 18th August, 2026 As per Ministry of Power (MoP) order, term of Appointment will be for a period of 05 (five) years w.e.f. the date of his assumption of charge of the post, or until further orders, whichever is earlier. Brief profile (in case of appointment); Shri Amol Babulal Taori (DIN: 11890590) is a Chartered Accountant with nearly 30 years of rich and diverse experience across Finance, Treasury, International Trade, Marketing, and Compensation Management. Prior to his appointment as Director (Finance), POWERGRID, Shri Taori served as Executive Director (In - charge) – International Trade at Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Limited (HPCL), where he managed crude procurement of approximately 700 kbd, product imports and exports, chartering/shipping arrangements, and oil price risk management. During his career, Shri Taori has managed one of India’s largest corporate treasuries for over a decade and spearheaded HPCL’s maiden USD bond issue, achieving one of the most competitive pricing spreads by an Indian issuer. He also conceptualised the Oil Bond Swap, which helped reduce borrowing costs, and facilitated HPCL’s first foreign currency swaps and revolving line of credit. He represented HPCL at global equity and debt roadshows, contributing significantly to strengthening investor confidence. He has also been a Trustee of all the employee benefits trusts of HPCL. Shri Taori has also served as a Director on the Board of HPCL Middle East FZCO, Dubai. Disclosure of relationships between directors (in case of appointment of a director). None",
