      "text": "19th August, 2026 Listing Department, National Stock Exchange Limited Exchange Plaza, C-1 Block-G Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra (E), Mumbai – 400 051 Symbol: HECPROJECT ISIN: INE558R01013 Sub: Submission of Newspaper clippings - Advertisement of Notice of AGM & E-voting Further to our letter dated 18 th August, 2026 submitting therewith Notice of Annual General Mee ting and Annual Report, we are enclosing herewith clippings of Newspapers Advertisement published on 19th August, 2026 for your information and records. This is in due compliance of the relevant Regulations of the SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015. Thanking you, Yours faithfully, For HEC INFRA PROJECTS LIMITED KHUSHI BHATT COMPANY SECRETARY M.NO: A51011 CMYK CMYK 7 Business AHMEDABAD WEDNESDAY 19/8/2026 Razorpay Launches Vulcan, India's First AI Payments Foundation Model Bangalore, India’s digital payments story has been one of growth and innovation - yet a quieter gap remains: a payment that doesn't go through, an OTP that arrives late, a subscription that silently lapses, a card compromised by fraud. For millions of first-time or small-town shoppers, one such experience is often enough to send them back to cash. Today, Razorpay, India's Omnichannel Payments Platform for Businesses, announced the launch of the Razorpay Vulcan, India's First Transformer-based AI Foundation Model built for payments, designed to make every digital payment in India more reliable, safer, and predictable. Built with NVIDIA and AWS technology, it combines Razorpay's payments data powered by NVIDIA's accelerated computing and A WS's cloud infrastructure - groundwork that India's e-commerce market needs as it heads toward a projected $350 bn by 2030. Harshil Mathur, CEO & Founder of Razorpay, said, “India's appetite for digital payments is real, but it isn't universal yet - for a large part of the country, going digital still comes down to one thing: does it work, every single time? That's the customer we built this for: the one still deciding whether to trust a screen over cash in hand. An AI-led payments foundation model doesn't just solve today's problem and stop there. Every payment teaches the system something that makes the next payment better. ” Pahal Patangia, Head of Global Industry Business Development and Payments, NVIDIA said, “India’s rapidly evolving digital economy is creating an opportunity to make payments more intelligent, reliable, and secure. NVIDIA’s work with Razorpay in partnership with AWS on AI payments foundation models has opened up a new frontier, turning complex payments data into real-time contextual intelligence. ” Kiran Jagannath, Head of FSI and Conglomerates, AWS India and South Asia, said, \"Razorpay is reimagining payments intelligence at India scale with an AI Foundation Model - built on Amazon SageMaker - that consolidates billions of transaction insights into a single, continuously learning intelligence layer, replacing fragmented ML models with unified AI that delivers higher payment success rates, rapid iteration, and enterprise-grade security for mission-critical payment flows.” HEC INFRA PROJECTS LIMITED NOTICE FOR 21ST ANNUAL GENERAL MEETING, AND E-VOTING [CIN: L45200GJ2005PLC046870] Registered Office: Sigma 1 Corporate, Corporate House No.6, Sindhu Bhawan Road, Nr. Mann Party Plot Cross road, Bodakdev, Ahmedabad – 380 054 NOTICE is hereby given that the 21st Annual General Meeting (“AGM”) of the members of the Company will be held on Friday, the 18th September, 2026 at 12.00 PM IST through Video Conference (“VC”)/ Other Audio Visual Means (“OAVM”) to transact the businesses as set out in the Notice dated 23rd July, 2026 convening the AGM. in accordance with the Circular issued by the Ministry of Corporate Affairs (\"MCA\") General Circular No. 03/2025 dated 22nd September, 2025 read with the requirements specified in Paragraphs 3 and 4 of General Circular No. 20/ 2020 dated 5th May, 2020 and other relevant circulars issued by MCA in this regard. Accordingly, the Company has sent the Annual Report 2025-26 along with the Notice convening AGM through electronic mode only to the members whose email addresses are registered with the Company and/or Depositories. The Annual Report along with the Notice convening the AGM is also available on the website of Company at - www.hecprojects.in and on the website of Central Depository Services (India) Limited at www.evotingindia.com and also on website of NSE Limited at www.nseindia.com. As per the Section 108 of the Comp anies Act, 2013 read with Rule 20 of the Companies (Management and Administration) Rules, 2014 and Regulation 44 of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015, the Company is providing its members the facilities to cast their vote by ‘Remote e-voting’ as under and also ‘e-voting’ at the time of AGM on all the resolutions set forth in the said Notice. The details as required pursuant to the provisions of the Companies Act, 2013 and Rules made there under are given here under. Place : Ahmedabad Date : 18th August, 2026 By Order of the Board for HEC INFRA PROJECTS LIMITED Khushi Bhatt Company Secretary & Compliance Officer 1 Date of completion of 18th August, 2026 dispatch of Notice of AGM through email only 2 Date & Time of commencement 9.00 a.m. on 15th September, 2026 of Remote e-voting 3 Date & Time of end of 5:00 p.m. on 17th September, 2026 Remote e-voting 4 Cut-off date for determining 11th September, 2026 rights of entitlement of Remote e-voting 5 Those persons who have acquired shares and have become members of the Company after emailing of notice of AGM by the Company and whose names appear in the Register of Me mbers of the Company/ in the statement of beneficial owners maintained by de positories as on cut-off date can exercise their voting rights through Remote e-voting by following the procedure as mentioned in the said Notice of AGM. 6 Remote e-voting shall After 5:00 p.m. on 17th September, 2026 not be allowed beyond 7 Manner of casting e-votes on E-voting facility will be available during AGM. Members resolutions during AGM who have already cast their vote by remote e-voting prior (VC/OAVM) to the AGM may remain present at AGM through VC/OAVM but shall not be entitled to cast their e-vote again during AGM. 8 Electronic Voting system & Central Depository Services (India) Limited VC/OAVM platform provider www .evotingindia.com 9 Contact details of person Mr. Rakesh Dalvi, Manager responsible to address the Central Depository Services (India) L imited grievances connected with 34/35th Floor, A Wing, Marathon Future x, e-voting system Mafatlal Mills Compound, NM Joshi Marg, Lower Parel (E), Mumbai - 400 013 E Mail ID -helpdesk.evoting@cdslindia.com Phone No. - 18002109911 NOTICE FOR 42ND ANNUAL GENERAL MEETING AND E-VOTING [CIN: L25200GJ1985PLC007746] Registered Office: 12th Floor, 1201, City Centre-2, B/S Heer Party Plot, Nr. Shukan mall Cross Road, Science City Road, Ahmedabad-380060 NOTICE is hereby given that the 42nd Annual General Meeting (“A GM”) of the members of the Company will be held on Monday, the 14th September, 2026 at 3.00 p.m. IST through Video Conference (“VC”)/ Other Audio Visual Means (“OAVM”) to transact the businesses, as set out in the Notice dated 29th July, 2026 convening the AGM. in accordance with the Circular issued by the Ministry of Corporate Affairs, (\"MCA\") General Circular No. 03/2025 dated 22nd September, 2025 read with the requirements specified in Paragraphs 3 and 4 of General Circular No. 20/2020 dated 5th May, 2020 and other relevant circulars issued by MCA in this regard. Accordingly, the Company has sent the Annual Report 2025-26 along with the Notice convening AGM through electronic mode only to the members whose email add resses are registered with the Company and/or Depositories.The Annual Report along with the Notice convening the AGM is also available on the website of Company at - www.promactimpex. com and on the website of Central Depository Services (India) Limited at www.evotingindia.com and also on website of BSE Limited at www.bseindia.com. As per the Section 108 of the Companies Act, 2013 read with Rule 20 of the Companies (Management and Administration) Rules, 2014 and Regulation 44 of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015, the Company is providing its members the facilities to cast their vote by ‘Remote e-voting’ as under and also ‘evoting’ at the time of AGM on all the resolutions set forth in the said Notice. The details as required pursuant to the provisions of the Companies Act, 2013 and Rules made there under are given here under: Place : Ahmedabad Date : 18th August, 2026 By Order of the Board For PROMACT PLASTICS LIMITED Ankit J. Patel Managing Director 1 Date of completion of 18th August, 2026 dispatch of Notice of AGM through email only 2 Date & Time of commencement 9.00 a.m. on 11th September, 2026 of Remote e-voting 3 Date & Time of end of 5:00 p.m. on 13th September, 2026 Remote e-voting 4 Cut-off date for determining 7th September, 2026 rights of entitlement of Remote e-voting 5 Those persons who have acquired shares and have become members of the Company after emailing of notice of AGM by the Company and whose names appear in the Register of Me mbers of the Company/ in the statement of beneficial owners maintained by de positories as on cut-off date can exercise their voting rights through Remote e-voting by followi ng the procedure as mentioned in the said Notice of AGM. 6 Remote e-voting shall After 5:00 p.m. on 13th September, 2026 not be allowed beyond 7 Manner of casting e-votes on E-voting facility will be available during AGM. Members resolutions during AGM who have already cast their vote by remote e-voting prior (VC/OAVM) to the AGM may remain present at AGM through VC/OAVM but shall not be entitled to cast their e-vote again during AGM. 8 Electronic Voting system & Central Depository Services (India) Limited VC/OAVM platform provider www .evotingindia.com 9 Contact details of person Mr. Rakesh Dalvi, Manager responsible to address the Central Depository Services (India) L imited grievances connected with 34/35thFloor, A Wing, Marathon Futurex , e-voting system Mafatlal Mills Compound, NM Joshi Marg, Lower Parel (E), Mumbai - 400 013 E Mail ID -helpdesk.evoting@cdslindia.com Phone No. - 18002109911 PROMACT PLASTICS LIMITED (formerly known as Promact Impex Limited) Business Brief JIO REINTRODUCES JIO PRIME WITH 1-YEAR PRICE GURANTEE Mumbai, Jio Prime Membership Programme was originally created as an act of gratitude to Jio’s first 100 million customers. Today, it is reintroduced to provide assurance of price guarantee and a range of additional benefits, for Jio’s family of over 500 million users. Jio Prime enables additional price certainty for future so that customers can continue recharging with confidence, their preferred eligible Jio plans at today's prices, irrespective of any future price revisions during the price-guarantee period, for one-year until 5 September 2027. Care Health Insurance Issues Public Health Advisory on Mosquito-Borne Diseases Mumbai, With monsoon increasing the risk of mosquito-borne diseases such as dengue, malaria, and chikungunya, Care Health Insurance has issued a public health advisory urging citizens to stay vigilant, adopt preventive measures and seek timely medical attention. While these diseases are largely preventable, they pose a recurring public health challenge during the monsoon, often resulting in serious illness and unplanned medical expenses. As India enters the peak monsoon season, public health authorities have intensified preparedness measures to minimise the impact of seasonal outbreaks. According to the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, all States and Union Territories have been advised to strengthen disease surveillance, vector control, community awareness, and healthcare preparedness. Under the same scenario, hospitals devise means to ensure adequate availability of beds, medicines, diagnostics, blood components, and trained healthcare personnel to effectively manage any surge in cases that may arise. Maruti's 'FRONX' becomes fastest Indian SUV to hit 2 lakh exports New Delhi, Aug 18 (IANS) Leading automobile firm Maruti Suzuki India Limited on Tuesday said that its popular SUV -- FRONX -- has crossed the milestone of 2 lakh exports in under 38 months, becoming the fastest SUV from India to achieve this feat. Exports of the Made-inIndia FRONX began in June 2023 and the model achieved its first lakh exports in under 25 months before adding the second lakh in about 13 months, the company said in a statement. Manufactured at Maruti Suzuki’s Hansalpur facility in Gujarat, FRONX is being exported to nearly 90 countries, including Japan, the statement added.“Every vehicle exported by Maruti Suzuki carries the hard work and pride of our people. These vehicles take a piece of Indian manufacturing to nearly 120 countries. FRONX has been a key contributor to Maruti Suzuki’s success in exports. Since FY 24-25, it has been India's No. 1 exported passenger vehicle,” Hisashi Takeuchi, Managing Director & CEO, Maruti Suzuki India Limited, said.\"After crossing the milestone of 1 lakh exports in record time, FRONX reached its second lakh significantly faster, underlining its growing demand in the international markets,\" Takeuchi said.He added that Maruti Suzuki continues to showcase the prowess of India’s manufacturing ecosystem aligned with ‘Make in India, Make for the World’. NRAI’s 5th Food Delivery Summit Highlights Gujarat as a New Growth Hub for India’s Restaurant Industry Ahmedabad, 18 August 2026: Ahead of the 5th NRAI Food Delivery Summit 2026, India’s biggest food business summit, the National Rest aurant Association of India (NRAI) today highlighted Gujarat as an increasingly important market for India’s restaurant and food services industry, with growth extending across Ahmedabad, Vadodara, Surat and Rajkot and new opportunities emerging around GIFT City. The observations were shared at a press conference in Ahmedabad ahead of the summit, which will be held on 20 August. Gujarat’s restaurant landscape has developed well beyond its traditional food culture. Ahmedabad alone has more than 20,000 restaurants, including cafés and QSRs, with the city’s restaurant sector estimated to be growing at 10–12% annually. Across Ahmedabad, Vadodara, Surat and Rajkot, NRAI has 500+ members, reflecting the breadth of the state’s restaurant ecosystem like The Secret Kitchen, Gopi Dining Hall, Old School Eatery, 22nd Parallel and Jagdish Foods to brands such as La Pino’z and Baskin-Robbins amongst many other leading F&B Brands. The market is seeing growing acceptance of premium dining, international cuisines, cafés, QSRs and experience-led formats, while businesses originating in Gujarat are increasingly building a presence beyond the state with the potential to scale across India and international markets. SEMICON India 2026 in Delhi to Accelerate India’s Semiconductor Ecosystem New Delhi, August 18, 2026: The fifth edition of SEMICON India 2026 will be held from September 17–19 at Yashobhoomi, New Delhi, and will be inaugurated by Hon’ble Prime Minister Narendra Modi. The event will bring together global semiconductor leaders, policymakers, industry experts, startups, and academia on a single platform. India’s semiconductor sector is gaining strong momentum under the India Semiconductor Mission (ISM), with 12 projects approved under Semicon 1.0. The announcement of Semicon 2.0 is set to further strengthen a robust and resilient ecosystem in the country. The government continues to support innovation and design through initiatives for academic institutions and startups. Shri S. Krishnan, Secretary, MeitY, said, “The success of the Semicon India Programme and the launch of Semicon 2.0 reflect India’s strong commitment to this sector. These initiatives will help position India as a global semiconductor hub.” Mr. Ashok Chandak (?????), President, SEMI India & IESA, added, “SEMICON India has become a key platform for collaboration and partnerships across the industry. The ‘Silicon to Systems’ theme highlights India’s growing capabilities across the semiconductor value chain.” Visitor registration is now open at: https://portal.semiconindia.org/register IMTMA to organise Pune Machine Tool Expo (PMTX) & Factory Equipment Expo (FACTEQ) 2026 at Pune Ahmedabad, 18 August 2026: Indian Machine Tool Manufacturers’ Association (IMTMA) will organise Pune Machine Tool Expo (PMTX) 2026, co-located with Factory Equipment Expo (FACTEQ) 2026 from 7 to 10 September 2026 at the Pune International Exhibition & Convention Centre (PIECC), Moshi, Pune. The announcement was made at a press conference held today in Ahmedabad. PMTX is a premier B2B exhibition that showcases advanced machine tools, manufacturing technologies, factory automation, and precision engineering solutions. FACTEQ is an exclusive exhibition on factory equipment focusing on products and solutions to meet the requirements of new factories and those that necessitate upgrading existing facilities. Over 175 exhibitors will display machine tools, metal cutting, metal forming, tooling, automation, robotics, metrology, and digital manufacturing technologies. Factory equipment, material handling, industrial infrastructure, energyefficient systems, and smart factory solutions will also be showcased. Business visitors from various industry segments such as automotive, aerospace, general and heavy engineering, capital goods, and many other sectors are expected to visit. Pune is one of India’s most important manufacturing and engineering centres. The expo is designed to provide the machine tool and manufacturing industry with a platform to evaluate solutions, interact with experts, and experience machines and factory systems LIVE. The expo will help visitors to get acquainted with the production technologies and factory infrastructure solutions. According to Mr. Jibak Dasgupta, Director General & ",
