      "url": "https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/SHREEDIG_20082026194621_81st_Annual_Report_FY_2025-26_signed.pdf",
      "text": "20th August ,2026 BSE Limited Corporate Relationship Department P.J. Towers Dalal Street Mumbai – 400 001 Company Code: 502180 National Stock Exchange of India Limited Exchange Plaza, Bandra Kurla Complex Bandra (East) Mumbai 400 051 Company Code: SHREDIGCEM Dear Sir / Madam, Sub: Submission of 81st Annual Report and Cut -off date for E - Voting & Remote E -Voting of Shree Digvijay Cement Company Ltd. (the “Company”). Ref : Our Letters dated 29th April, 2026 and 24th July, 2026 Further to our Letters dated 29th April,2026 and 24th July,2026, we would like to inform that the Eighty-first (81st) Annual General Meeting (“AGM”) of the Company will be held as under: Day and Date : Wednesday, 16th September,2026 Time: 11:00 A.M. (IST) Mode : Through Video Conference (“VC”) / Other Audio-Visual Means (“OAVM”) Venue : The proceedings of the AGM shall be deemed to be conducted at the Registered Office of the Company at P.O. Digvijaygram – 361 140, Via Jamnagar, Gujarat, India. Pursuant to Regulation 34(1) of Securities Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 (“SEBI Listing Regulations”), please find herewith the 81st Annual Report of the Company along with the Notice of the 81st AGM of the Company for the financial year 2025-26 which is being sent through electronic mode to the Members. The Annual Report containing the Notice of AGM is also uploaded on the Company’s website, at weblink; https://www.digvijaycement.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/81st-Annual-Report-FY-2025-26.pdf Cut-off date for E-Voting & Remote E-Voting Period:- The Members, whose names appear in the Register of Members / Beneficial Owners as on the record date (cut-off date) i.e. Wednesday, 9th September, 2026, will be entitled to cast their vote electronically. The remote e -voting period begins on Saturday, 12th September, 2026 at 9:00 A.M. (IST) and ends on Tuesday, 15th September, 2026 at 5:00 P.M. (IST). We request you to kindly take the above submission on Record. Thanking you, Yours faithfully, For Shree Digvijay Cement Company Limited Suresh Meher Sr. VP (Legal) & Company Secretary Encl.: As above SHREE DIGVIJAY CEMENT COMPANY LIMITED ANNUAL REPORT 2025-26 81 st BUILT ON PARTNERSHIP. DRIVEN BY GROWTH. Customer Delight Empowering People Building Trusted Partnerships Sustainable Business Practices Shree Digvijay Cement Company Limited stands to be a trusted building materials organization creating value for every stakeholder through excellence. Over the last 81 years, we have strived tirelessly, in a way that creates long term value and excellence through: RESPONSIBLITY We are accountable for all our actions and are committed to transparency INNOVATION We value innovation in pursuit of excellence SUSTAINABILITY We believe in sustainable and socially responsible practices ETHICS We value integrity and good governance UNITY We are one company, one team, creating immense value for our stakeholders PEOPLE We value people by respecting all individuals and their contributions Our values are best represented by our continuous efforts to UPRISE 81ST ANNUAL REPORT 2025-26 01 COMPANY OVERVIEW Board of Directors .......................................................02 F rom the Desk of Chairman .......................................03 Corpor ate Information ................................................04 10-years Financial Highlights & Key Financial Indicators .............................................05 09 NOTICE & REPORTS Notice to the Members ...............................................09 Direct ors’ Report .......................................................26 Management Discussion & Analysis .........................50 ESG Initiatives and Achie vements .............................57 Corpor ate Governance Report....................................63 Business Responsibility & Sustainability Report ...................................................84 TABLE OF CONTENTS 119 FINANCIAL STATEMENTS STANDALONE Independent A uditors’ Report ..................................119 Balance Sheet .....................................................128 Statement of Profit and Loss ...................................129 Cash Flow Statement................................................130 Statement of Change in Equity.................................132 Notes to Accounts ....................................................133 CONSO LIDATED Independent Auditors’ Report ..................................184 Balance Sheet .....................................................190 Statement of Profit and Loss ...................................191 Cash Flow Statement................................................192 Statement of Change in Equity.................................194 Notes to Accounts .................................................... 195 F orm AOC-1 ...............................................................248 81st ANNUAL REPORT 2025-26 2 SHREE DIGVIJAY CEMENT COMPANY LIMITED BOARD OF DIRECTORS Ms. Mitu is the Founder of Eminence Strategy Consulting, a company which works with organisations and individuals in building, establishing and protecting their reputation through stakeholder engagement. She has over two decades of experience in brand positioning and reputation management. She also serves as a director on the boards of several other public companies. As a certified leadership coach, she actively coaches C-Suite leaders on making their presence impactful. She has authored several articles and regularly speaks at various industry forums. Ms. Mitu has pursued a Master’s in Economics from Mumbai University and holds a Management degree in Business Administration from SP Jain Institute of Management & Research. Ms. Mitu Samarnarth Jha Independent Director Mr. Singhvi has vast experience in managing and running large corporates, including, long experience in cement and other industries in India. He is a Chartered Accountant and having outstanding professional career. Out of over 44 years of experience, he spent 23 years in building up of Ambuja Cement, where the last position held by him was of the CEO and Managing Director. Mr. Singhvi was awarded Entrepreneur Finalist Award by EY in 2006, and best CFO award by ET. Mr. Anil Singhvi Executive Chairman Mr. Gupta has more than 4 decades of professional experience in the areas of Business Management and all dimensions of finance, M&As, Company Law, taxation etc. In his career, he has played a critical role as a key strategist in turning around companies and guiding them to achieve new heights through his insights. Currently he is the Group Advisor to Ashok Piramal Group and has been associated with this group for about 21 years (Including 14 years as Group Managing Director). Earlier, Mr. Gupta was Group CFO and Management Board Member of RPG Group and Piramal Enterprises. Mr. Gupta has received a number of recognitions including CFO of the Year Award (for special commendation for Financial Excellence in M&A Category). He holds Honours Degree in B.Com; L.L.B (Gen), a Chartered Accountant and a Company Secretary. Mr. Mahesh Gupta Independent Director Mr. Satish Kulkarni has rich experience of over 33 years in B2B business, consumer services, channel sales, brand management and marketing. He was Chairman on the Board of SCIB PAINTS, responsible to steer the Board of Egyptian subsidiary of Asian Paints Group. Mr. Satish Kulkarni had joined Asian Paints Ltd. in 1993 and held various positions at Asian Paints, prior to joining the Company’s Board in June, 2020. Presently, he works as a Board Member or Board Advisory for a set of companies from diverse industry sectors. He is a B.E. (Electronics) from Walchand College of Engineering, Sangli; and PGDBM from IIM, Ahmedabad. Mr. Satish Kulkarni Independent Director Mr. Amit Arora brings with him over two decades of rich experience in the cement industry and has held various strategic leadership roles across the value chain, including Plant Head with ACC Limited. Most recently, he was Plant Head at Vicat Group’s Kalaburgi Cement. He has also been part of global leadership, business excellence, technical and digital transformation programs conducted by Holcim Group. His core expertise encompasses plant operations, P&L management, supply chain optimization, digital transformation and sustainable business growth. Mr. Arora holds a B.Tech in Mechanical Engineering and MBA from Indian Institute of Management (IIM) Indore. Mr. Amit Arora CEO & Managing Director Mr. Shitij Kale has over two decades of experience in investments, encompassing both buy-side and sell-side roles. He has led complex strategic, mergers and acquisitions, and capital market transactions across multiple sectors. He previously headed M&A for the transportation and consumer verticals at the Adani Group, overseeing transactions across ports, airports, logistics, roads, city gas distribution, FMCG, and consumer technology. Prior thereto, he led the Infrastructure and Energy Investment Banking practice at Citigroup India, advising on strategic M&A and capital-raising transactions across infrastructure, oil and gas, chemicals, and industrial sectors. He has also worked in corporate credit at DCB Bank. Mr. Kale has extensive experience across the investment lifecycle, including origination, structuring, execution, and monetisation, with a focus on value creation, strategic initiatives, and capital management, and has served on the boards of several companies. He holds a Master’s degree in Business Administration (Finance), is a CFA (India) charter holder, and is a Chemical Engineer. Mr. Shitij Kale Non-Executive Director SHREE DIGVIJAY CEMENT COMPANY LIMITED 3 FROM THE DESK OF CHAIRMAN Dear Fellow Members, It’s my pleasure to share with you an overview of our Company’s journey during 2025 - 26, a year marked by transformation, resilience, and strategic progress. A defining highlight of the year was the successful installation and commissioning of our new grinding unit. This milestone has significantly expanded our cement production capacity, enhanced operational efficiency, and improved product quality. It positions us more competitively in the cement market while reflecting our commitment to modern infrastructure, sustainability, and cost effective growth. Equally transformative was the strategic integration with Hi Bond Cement (India) Private Limited under the Brand Usage, Supply, and Distributorship Agreement. Effective 19th March 2026, this partnership has enabled us to purchase and distribute Hi Bond’s cement products, thereby expanding our product portfolio and strengthening our distribution franchise. The synergy of this integration, combined with our expanded capacity, has elevated our market reach to over 5 million tonnes, firmly positioning Shree Digvijay Cement among the top three cement players in Gujarat. The year also saw changes in the promoter our erstwhile promoters, True North Fund VI LLP sold their shares to IRF Group. Our teams are excited about the growth opportunity & making Kamal & Hi-Bond brands as number one brands in Saurashtra. In conclusion, I extend my sincere gratitude to our shareholders, employees, customers, and partners for their unwavering support and trust. Together, we will continue to build a stronger, more resilient, and forward looking organization. Best Regards, Yours sincerely, Anil Singhvi SHREE DIGVIJAY CEMENT COMPANY LIMITED BOARD COMMITTEES AUDIT COMMITTEE Mr. Mahesh Gupta (Chairman) Mr. Satish Kulkarni Mr. Shitij Kale NOMINATION AND REMUNERATION COMMITTEE Ms. Mitu Samarnath Jha (Chairperson) Ms. Satish Kulkarni Mr. Shitij Kale STAKEHOLDERS RELATIONSHIP COMMITTEE Ms. Mitu Samarnath Jha (Chairperson) Mr. Shitij Kale Mr. Anil Singhvi CORPORATE SOCIAL RESPONSIBILITY COMMITTEE Mr. Satish Kulkarni (Chairman) Mr. Anil Singhvi Mr. Shitij Kale Mr. Amit Arora RISK MANAGEMENT COMMITTEE Mr. Mahesh Gupta (Chairman) Mr. Satish Kulkarni Mr. Shitij Kale REGISTERED OFFICE AND WORKS P .O. Digvijaygram – 361 140 Via. Jamnagar (Gujarat) Tel. (0288) 2344 272 – 2344 275; Fax No. (0288) 2344 092 E-mail: investors.sdccl@digvijaycement.com Website: www.digvijaycement.com CORPORATE INFORMATION CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER Mr. Vikas Kumar - President & Chief Financial Officer COMPANY SECRETARY & COMPLIANCE OFFICER Mr. Suresh Kumar Meher Senior Vice President (Legal) & Company Secretary OTHER SENIOR MANAGEMENT TEAM Dr. Girish Mehta - Senior Vice President (MRM & Logistics) Mr. Thiyaku Narayanasamy - Vice President (Plant) AUDITORS BSR and Co. Chartered Accountants COST AUDITORS M/s Kiran J. Mehta & Co. INTERNAL AUDITORS M/s RSM Astute Consulting Private Limited SECRETARIAL AUDITORS M/s. Manoj Hurkat & Associates REGISTRAR AND SHARE TRANSFER AGENT M/s MUFG Intime India Private Limited CORPORATE IDENTIFICATION NUMBER L26940GJ1944PLC000749 SHREE DIGVIJAY CEMENT COMPANY LIMITED 81st ANNUAL REPORT 2025-264 FINANCIAL STATEMENTSNOTICE & REPORTSCOMPANY OVERVIEW SHREE DIGVIJAY CEMENT COMPANY LIMITED 5 (All Amounts are in ` Lakhs, unless otherwise stated) IND AS OPERATING RESULTS Mar '26 Mar '25 Mar '24 Mar '23 Mar '22 Mar '21 Mar '20 Mar '19 Mar '18 Mar '17 Total Revenue (Net of Excise Duty / Net of GST) 75,315 73,499 80,097 73,192 63,333 50,914 47,209 44,111 41,972 32,704 Material Cost 18,714 17,255 15,092 12,462 11,170 9,639 8,152 9,901 10,268 6,923 Employee Benefit Expenses 4,288 4,193 4,073 3,895 3,767 3,662 3,439 2,899 2,694 2,627 Power & Fuel Cost 22,519 22,946 24,394 27,810 20,870 13,470 13,909 15,456 11,973 10,180 Other Expenses 22,335 22,399 21,043 18,265 15,420 13,007 11,394 12,738 11,617 10,992 Depreciation and Amortisation 3,125 2,975 3,462 3,526 3,140 2,683 2,480 2,399 2,288 2,219 Finance Cost 955 277 212 134 146 159 178 386 1,069 1,147 Profit Before Tax and Exceptional Items 3,381 3,455 11,821 7,100 8,820 8,294 7,657 332 2,063 -1,384 Exceptional Items - - - - - - - - - - Tax Expense 881 934 3,045 1,329 3,291 2,895 2,014 12