      "url": "https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DIACABS_22082026192713_Regulation_30-Receipt_of_Letter_of_Intent.pdf",
      "text": "DIAMOND POWER INFRASTRUCTURE LIMITED Regd. Office & Factory: Vadadala, Phase – II Savli, Vadodara, Gujarat, India-391520 CIN: L31300GJ1992PLC018198 Email: cs@dicabs.com, Website: www.dicabs.com Tel No.- 02667-251354/251516 Fax No.-02267-251202 August 22, 2026 To, The Manager – Listing Department BSE Limited Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai – 400 001 Scrip Code: 522163 To, The Manager – Listing Department National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. Exchange Plaza, C-1, Block G, BKC, Bandra (East), Mumbai – 400 051 Symbol: DIACABS Sub: Disclosure under Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 – Receipt of Letter of Intent / orders aggregating ₹52.86 crore crore placed by Aurionpro Solutions Limited for the supply of HT and LT electrical cables to a hyperscale data centre campus at Hyderabad Dear Sir/Madam, Pursuant to Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 (“Listing Regulations”), read with SEBI Master Circular on compliance with the provisions of the Listing Regulations by listed entities, we wish to inform you that Diamond Power Infrastructure Limited (\"the Company\") has received Letter of Intent / order, aggregating to ₹ 52.86 crore (including GST), from Aurionpro Solutions Limited for the supply of HT and LT electrical cables to a hyperscale data centre campus at Hyderabad. The details required under Regulation 30 of the Listing Regulations, read with the applicable SEBI Circular, are enclosed as Annexure A. A copy of the Press Release being issued by the Company in this regard is enclosed as Annexure B. This intimation is also being made available on the website of the Company at www.dicabs.com. You are requested to kindly take the above on record. Thanking you, Yours faithfully, For Diamond Power Infrastructure Limited Jayesh Patel Company Secretary ICSI M. No.: A14898 Encl.: Annexure A – Disclosure under Regulation 30; Annexure B – Press Release DIAMOND POWER INFRASTRUCTURE LIMITED Regd. Office & Factory: Vadadala, Phase – II Savli, Vadodara, Gujarat, India-391520 CIN: L31300GJ1992PLC018198 Email: cs@dicabs.com, Website: www.dicabs.com Tel No.- 02667-251354/251516 Fax No.-02267-251202 Annexure A Disclosure of details under Regulation 30 of the Listing Regulations read with the applicable SEBI Circular – Award / Receipt of Order Sr. Particulars Details 1 Name of the entity awarding the order / contract Aurionpro Solutions Limited 2 Nature of the order / contract Letter of Intent (LOI) from Aurionpro Solutions Limited for the supply of HT and LT electrical cables to a hyperscale data centre campus at Hyderabad 3 Whether order / contract awarded by domestic or international entity Domestic 4 Broad consideration / size of the order Aggregate order value: ₹52.86 crore (including GST) 5 Time period by which the order / contract is to be executed Supplies commence immediately and are scheduled on a staggered basis in line with the site's construction programme 6 Significant terms and conditions in brief It comprises approximately 130 kilometres of cable, of which over 116 kilometres is 1100 V grade, XLPE-insulated, FRLS-sheathed 1C x 300 sq mm copper conductor cable — the backbone distribution cable for high-density server halls. The balance covers 33 kV (E) grade aluminium XLPE armoured FRLS cable, 1.1 kV aluminium armoured LT power cables and copper control cables, all built to the client's IEC 61914 cleat and fire-performance specifications 7 Whether the promoter / promoter group / group companies have any interest in the entity that awarded the order / contract; if yes, nature of interest and details thereof No. The order has been received in the ordinary course of business and at arm’s length. 8 Whether the same would fall within related party transactions; if yes, whether at arm’s length No. The transaction does not fall within related party transactions. DIAMOND POWER INFRASTRUCTURE LIMITED Regd. Office & Factory: Vadadala, Phase – II Savli, Vadodara, Gujarat, India-391520 CIN: L31300GJ1992PLC018198 Email: cs@dicabs.com, Website: www.dicabs.com Tel No.- 02667-251354/251516 Fax No.-02267-251202 Annexure B PRESS RELEASE Diamond Power Infrastructure Limited receives Letter of Intent from Aurionpro Solutions for cable supply to Hyderabad data centre campus Vadodara, 22 August 2026 — Diamond Power Infrastructure Limited (NSE: DIACABS | BSE: 522163), one of India's integrated manufacturers of power cables and conductors operating under the DICABS brand, has received a Letter of Intent (LOI) from Aurionpro Solutions Limited (NSE: AURIONPRO | BSE: 532668) for the supply of HT and LT electrical cables to a hyperscale data centre campus at Hyderabad. The LOI, valued at approximately ₹52.86 crore (Including GST), covers the HYD-20 package of the campus, for which Aurionpro is the appointed EPC contractor. Supplies commence immediately and are scheduled on a staggered basis in line with the site's construction programme, delivered DAP Hyderabad. The contract is on a price-variation basis under the IEEMA formula with April 2026 base indices A copper-led order The package is overwhelmingly copper -intensive. It comprises approximately 130 kilometres of cable , of which over 116 kilometres is 1100 V grade, XLPE -insulated, FRLS-sheathed 1C x 300 sq mm copper conductor cable — the backbone distribution cable for high -density server halls. The balance covers 33 kV (E) grade aluminium XLPE armoured FRLS cable, 1.1 kV aluminium armoured LT power cables and copper control cables, all built to the client's IEC 61914 cleat and fire-performance specifications. The order draws directly on the copper wire drawing and copper cable manufacturing line recently commissioned by DICABS, which has a capacity of 1,500 MT of copper cables per month. The line was set up specifically to address high-intensity power applications such as data centres and power plants and marks the Company's entry into copper-based cables alongside its established aluminium cables and conductors’ business. Management comment Mr. Umesh Chayya, Whole time Director, Diamond Power Infrastructure Limited, said: \"Data centres are the single fastest-growing load centre in India, and they demand cable of a quality and consistency that very few plants in the country can deliver at scale. This order validates two things — the decision to invest in copper capability, and our ability to hold delivery schedules against a construction programme that moves week to week. We are supplying into this campus through more than one EPC partner, and we intend to be the reference cable supplier for India's data centre build-out,our Order book for Data Center at Present value exceeds Rs 575 cr – we expect to target this segment aggressively\" About Diamond Power Infrastructure Limited (DICABS) Diamond Power Infrastructure Limited is an integrated manufacturer of power cables and conductors, with a 130-acre manufacturing complex at Vadodara, Gujarat. The Company manufactures EHV, HV, MV and LV power cables, control and instrumentation cables, and a full range of aluminium and alloy conductors, backed by inDIAMOND POWER INFRASTRUCTURE LIMITED Regd. Office & Factory: Vadadala, Phase – II Savli, Vadodara, Gujarat, India-391520 CIN: L31300GJ1992PLC018198 Email: cs@dicabs.com, Website: www.dicabs.com Tel No.- 02667-251354/251516 Fax No.-02267-251202 house aluminium rod mills, a copper wire drawing line and captive wind power. DICABS serves transmission utilities, distribution companies, EPC contractors, industrial and infrastructure customers across India and overseas. This release contains forward-looking statements based on current expectations. Actual results may differ. Contract values stated are base prices; final realisation is subject to the applicable price variation formula. For further information, please contact: Jayesh Patel, Company Secretary & Compliance Officer Diamond Power Infrastructure Limited Email: cs@dicabs.com | www.dicabs.com Safe Harbour: Certain statements in this release concerning future prospects may be forward -looking statements. Actual results may differ materially from those expressed or implied. Order values stated are at base prices and are subject to price variation as per the applicable IEEMA formula and to final quantities as per site survey and customer approvals.",
      "error": "",
      "updatedAt": "23-Aug-2026 19:28 IST"
    },
