      "text": "(Formerly known as “Meesho Private Limited” and “Fashnear Technologies Private Limited”) CIN: L74900KA2015PLC082263 Registered Office: 3rd Floor, Wing-E, Helios Business Park, Kadubeesanahalli Village, Varthur Hobli, Outer Ring Road, Bengaluru, Karnataka 560103 T: +91 9108021923 | E: cs@meesho.com | W: www.meesho.com MEESHO LIMITED August 24, 2026 To, To, Listing Department Department of Corporate Services National Stock Exchange of India Limited BSE Limited Exchange Plaza, Bandra-Kurla Complex, Bandra (East), Mumbai - 400 051 Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai - 400 001 Symbol: MEESHO Scrip Code: 544632 Dear Sir / Madam, Subject: Notice of 11th Annual General Meeting and Annual Report for Financial Year 2025-26 Ref: Disclosure under Regulation 30 and 34(1) of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 as amended (“SEBI Listing Regulations”) Pursuant to Regulations 30 and 34(1) of the SEBI Listing Regulations, we wish to inform you that the 11th Annual General Meeting (“AGM”) of the Meesho Limited (the “Company”) is scheduled to be held on Friday, September 18, 2026, at 12:00 noon (IST) through Video Conferencing /Other Audio -Visual Means ( “VC/OAVM”), in accordance with the applicable circulars issued by the Ministry of Corporate Affairs and the Securities and Exchange Board of India. In this regard, please find enclosed the Annual Report of the Company for the Financial Year 2025 -26, including the Notice convening of the 11th AGM and other statutory reports. The Notice of the AGM and the Annual Report are being sent through electronic mode to those Members whose names appear in the Register of Members/List of Beneficial Owners as on Friday, August 21, 2026, and whose e-mail addresses are registered with the Co mpany/KFin Technologies Limited, the Registrar and Transfer Agent (“ KFin” or “ RTA”)/Depository Participant(s) (“DPs”)/Depositories. Further, in accordance with Regulation 36(1)(b) of the SEBI Listing Regulations, the Company is also sending a letter to those Members whose e -mail addresses are not registered with the Company/RTA/DPs/Depositories, providing the web -link and QR code to access the Annual Report and Notice of the AGM on the Company's website. The Company has engaged KFin as the agency for providing the e -voting facility. The Company is providing the facility of remote e-voting and e-voting during the AGM to its Members in respect of all the resolutions set forth in the Notice of the AGM. The Notice, inter alia, contains detailed instructions for remote e -voting, attending the AGM through VC/OAVM and registration of e-mail addresses by the Members. Members holding shares as on Friday, September 11, 2026, (“Cut-off date ”), shall be entitled to cast their votes electronically on the resolutions set out in the Notice of the AGM. The remote e-voting shall commence from 9:00 A.M. (IST) on Sunday, September 13, 2026, and shall remain open till 5:00 P.M. (IST) on Thursday, September 17, 2026. The aforesaid information including the Notice of the AGM and the Annual Report for the Financial Year 2025 -26 will also be made available on the Company’s website at: https://investor.meesho.com/ You are requested to take the above information on record. Thanking you, For Meesho Limited (Formerly known as Meesho Private Limited and Fashnear Technologies Private Limited) Rahul Bhardwaj Company Secretary and Compliance Officer Membership No.: A41649 Encl: As above Notice of the Annual General Meeting ...............................333 Particulars of Index Corporate Overview & Meesho’s Business Our Ecosystem .............05 Our Platform .................09 CEO’s Letter .......................12 CTO’s Letter .......................16 Board of Directors ................24 What we are building ..........02 Key Metrics ....................19 Our Transaction Model ......................11 Statutory Reports Management Discussion and Analysis ...........................................30 Board’s Report and its Annexures ...............................36 Corporate Governance Report ...........................70 Business Responsibility and Sustainability Report (BRSR) ....100 Financial Statements Independent Auditor’s Report on Consolidated Financial Statements ......................150 Consolidated Financial Statements .......................158 Independent Auditor’s Report on Standalone Financial Statements .......................241 Standalone Financial Statements ......................252 What We Are Building Who we are We are a multi-sided technology platform driving e-commerce in India, connecting four key stakeholders. Consumers Sellers Logistics Partners Content Creators Our platform is built to make e-commerce affordable, accessible, and engaging for all consumer segments, anchored on ‘Everyday Low Prices’. Technology-first operations and platform scale enable low-cost fulfilment for sellers, and combined with our zero-commission model, allow us to offer a wide assortment from unbranded and regional products to national brands at affordable prices. Our Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning (AI/ML)-led algorithms power a personalised, discovery-led shopping experience that mirrors offline window shopping, making online shopping easy and engaging. Technology is the backbone of our platform, enabling e-commerce at population scale across India. Our modular architecture orchestrates stakeholder interactions with reliability, scalability, and efficiency. Every interaction generates data that feeds our AI systems, powering hyper-personalised recommendations, dynamic pricing, automated cataloguing, transaction risk management, and logistics optimisation. We monetise through services provided to sellers from order fulfilment, advertising to data insights while charging no commission to sellers and no platform fees to consumers. Statutory Reports Financial StatementsCorporate OverviewMeesho Limited | Annual Report 2025-26 02 03 Our Mission Our mission is to democratise internet commerce for everyone. For us, that means removing the barriers that have historically limited participation in e-commerce. We believe access to e-commerce should not be determined by income levels, geography, language, or technical expertise. A consumer in a rural village should have the same depth of choice as one in the large city, rather than being limited to whatever the local market happens to stock. A business owner should be able to reach customers across India without significant upfront investment. A logistics entrepreneur or content creator should be able to participate in the growth of e-commerce regardless of scale. Each barrier we remove brings more people into the market, and over time that grows the market itself. Technology is the foundation that makes this possible. An accessible and affordable platform brings consumers, sellers, logistics partners and content creators into a single ecosystem where each participant strengthens the value proposition for the others; a new seller widens the choice a consumer sees, a new consumer enlarges the market a seller can reach, and a denser logistics network makes serving both cheaper and more reliable. Today, Meesho connects over 264 million Annual Transacting Users with more than 961k active sellers, supported by over 18k logistics partners, and 63k content creators across India. Together, they form one of the largest e-commerce ecosystems in the country and advance our mission of democratising internet commerce for everyone. Our Ecosystem Consumers Consumers are the starting point of the Meesho ecosystem. As more users transact on the platform, sellers gain access to a larger demand base, logistics partners benefit from higher volumes, and content creators find greater opportunities to engage and influence purchase decisions. Meesho remains India’s most downloaded shopping app, driven by our continued focus on accessibility and affordability for Bharat. Our Annual Transacting User base grew 33.0% YoY to 264 million in FY26, continuing a multi-year trend of accelerating user growth. A significant proportion of these users come from Tier 2+ markets, many of whom are participating in e-commerce for the first time. Our technology-led discovery experience, personalised recommendations, and content commerce ecosystem help consumers find relevant products, while our broad assortment spanning unbranded products, regional brands, and national brands through Meesho Mall ensures wide choice across price points. Combined with our focus on everyday low prices, this makes online commerce more accessible to Indians consumers. As trust in the platform grows, consumers expand into more categories and transact more frequently over time. This deepening engagement drives demand across the marketplace and advances our mission of democratising internet commerce for everyone. Annual Transacting Users 14.1% 27.7% 33.0% 136 156 199 264 (in million) Statutory Reports Financial StatementsCorporate OverviewMeesho Limited | Annual Report 2025-26 04 05 Sellers Our active seller base grew 87.0% YoY to 961k in FY26, reflecting the increasing attractiveness of Meesho as a platform for entrepreneurs across India. These sellers span a diverse range of categories including apparel, footwear and accessories, home, kitchen and furnishings, kids and baby products, and beauty and personal care. We pioneered a zero-commission model that enables sellers to participate in e-commerce without the commission structures traditionally charged by online marketplaces. Combined with low-cost order fulfilment, this makes Meesho one of the most economical platforms to sell on in India and lowers the barriers to entrepreneurship for businesses of all sizes. Logistics Partners Our logistics ecosystem comprises first and last mile delivery partners, sorting centres, truck operators, and end-to-end logistics providers. As order volumes on the platform continue to grow, logistics partners benefit from access to a large and expanding pool of e-commerce demand across India. Orders on Meesho are fulfilled either through Valmo, our proprietary technology platform that orchestrates fulfilment across a multi-partner logistics network, or directly through end-to-end logistics partners. By aggregating demand and intelligently routing shipments across multiple participants, Valmo improves asset utilisation and enables efficient fulfilment at scale. As more sellers join the platform, assortment expands, consumer choice improves, and the marketplace becomes increasingly relevant to a wider set of shopping needs. Our platform simplifies the selling journey, with AI-powered cataloguing, demand intelligence, and automated advertising solutions which help sellers improve discovery of their products and grow their business. Sellers also benefit from access to our creator ecosystem, which drives content-led product discovery and incremental demand for their listings. Importantly, Valmo lowers barriers to participation by allowing logistics providers without end-toend capabilities to participate in the growth of e-commerce. This expands earning opportunities for a broader set of logistics entrepreneurs while increasing network capacity, coverage, and resilience for the platform. As the logistics network grows, fulfilment becomes more efficient, delivery reach expands, and service quality improves for both consumers and sellers. Statutory Reports Financial StatementsCorporate OverviewMeesho Limited | Annual Report 2025-26 06 07 Content Creators As shopping becomes increasingly discovery-led, content has emerged as a powerful bridge between consumers and products. Rather than searching for a specific item, consumers are increasingly discovering products through videos, recommendations, and demonstrations that help build trust and purchase intent. Meesho enables this shift through its growing creator ecosystem. Content creators produce short-form videos on both the Meesho app and third-party platforms, helping consumers discover, evaluate, and purchase products in a more engaging and immersive manner. In turn, creators are able to monetise their influence by earning commissions on sales generated through their content. In FY26, we enabled 63,213 Active Content Creators who generated over 1.4 million pieces of order-generating content on a cumulative basis. As our creator ecosystem expands, consumers benefit from richer product discovery experiences while sellers gain new channels to reach and convert potential customers. Our Platform Our platform is built on multiple scaled self-reinforcing flywheels orchestrating transactions amongst our four key stakeholders. Commerce Flywheel At the core of our platform is our commerce flywheel. Consumers transact on Meesho because of the wide assortment of products that are available at affordable prices. As more consumers transact and order volumes increase, more sellers are attracted to Meesho. This encourages sellers to list more products on Meesho and price their products competitively. Logistics Flywheel As order volumes on Meesho increase, it helps logistics partners better utilise their capacity, improve the density of fulfilment, and reduce the price of their services on a per-order basis. On Valmo (the technology of which is housed in our Company), logistics partners who may not have been able to service e-commerce orders because they did not have end-to-end capabilities, can come together to jointly service e-commerce orders. With reducing fulfilment costs, we are able to reduce the average cost charged to sellers, enabling them to price their products more competitively and list lower-value products on Meesho, which in turn attracts more consumers. Content Commerce Flywheel We have activated a content commerce flywheel that enhances product discovery and engagement on Meesho. Content creators are attracted to Meesho as we offer them an avenue to monetise their creativity by promoting our sellers’ products. With increasing content volumes on Meesho, product discovery becomes better, further increasing order volumes and reinforcing the commerce flywheel. Statutory Reports Financial StatementsCorporate OverviewMeesho Limited | Annual Report 2025-26 08 09 120k Valmo Delivery Agents 18k Active Logistics Providers 5 End-to-End Logistics Partners 961k Annual Transacting Sellers 63k Active Content Creators 264 Mn Annual Transacting Users Better Pricing and Assortments More Orders Commerce Flywheel Content Commerce Flywheel Logistics FlywheelMore Sellers Low Cost Better Discovery More Consumers Our Transaction Model Consumers pay via prepaid or cash on delivery, with no platform fees charged, consistent with our goal of making e-commerce affordable and accessible. We charge sellers no commissions, only fees for services such as order fulfilment, returns, and advertisements. Logistics partners handle pickup, transportation, and last-mile delivery, with fulfilment fees collected from sellers (reported under Revenue from operations – Marketplace) and paid out based on parcel weight, distance, and payment mode. Content creators drive product discovery and conversion for sellers, who pay us a content service fee reported under the same revenue line, while payments to creators — based on orders generated — are reported under advertising and sales promotion expenses. Note: (1) Checkout value on aggregate is NMV; (2) Factors such as weight of parcel, distance, mode of payment, among others. Checkout Value Less (i) Fee For Services Provided (ii) Applicable Tax Checkout Value1 Fee For Services Provided Order Fulfilment Costs Based On Order Parameters 2 Content Related Costs As % Of NMV Generated (Order Fulfilment, Advertisements, Content Commerce and Others) Sellers Consumers Logistics Partners Content Creators More Creators and Content More Logistics Partners Statutory Reports Financial StatementsCorporate OverviewMeesho Limited | Annual Report 2025-26 10 11",
