      "text": "@ NCREDIBLE INDUSTRIES LIMITED An ISO 9001:2015, 14001:2015 & 45001:2018 Organisation ' Corporate Office : “LANSDOWNE TOWERS”, 2/1A, SARAT BOSE ROAD, KOLKATA - 700 020 PH. : 033-6638 4700 * FAX : 91-33-6638 4729 x Website : www.incredibleindustries.co.in E-mail : incredibleindustries1979@iilgroup.co.in EHAROSA HAMESHA 25% August, 2026. Listing Department The Secretary BSE Limited National Stock Exchange of India Limited Phiroze Jeejecbhoy Towers Exchange Plaza, Bandra Kurla Complex Dalal Street Bandra (E) Mumbai400 001. Mumbai-400 051. Scrip Code: 538365 Scrip CodeINCREDIBLE The Secretary The Calcutta Stock Exchange Limited 7, Lyons Range Kolkata-700 001 Scrip Code: 28188 Dear Sir/ Madam, Sub: Submission of 47\" Annual Report of the Company for the Financial Year 2025-26 along with notice of 47\" Annual General Meeting Re: Regulation 34 of the SEBI (Listing Regulations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 In accordance with Regulation 34 of the SEBI (Listing Regulations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, please find enclosed herewith 47\" Annual Report of the Company for the financial year 2025-26 along with notice of 47\" Annual General Meeting of the Company to be held on Friday, 18\" September, 2026 at 02:30 P.M. through Video Conferencing / Other Audio Visual Means (“VC/OAVM). The Annual Report and notice has also been made available on the website of the Company at wwiwv.ineredibleindustries.co.in . Thanking you and assuring you of our best attention always, Yours faithfully, For Incredible Industries Limited Company Secretary and Compliance Officer Name: Bharat Agarwal M. No.- FCS-11144 Encl.: As mentioned above Regd. Office : 14, Netaji Subhas Road, I1-Floor, Kolkata - 700 001 ® : 2243-4355, 2242-8551 Works : Raturia, Angadpur, Durgapur - 713 215, Phone : (0343) 2591105/2591122/1123/1124 CIN : L27100WB1979PLC032200 What’s Inside 1 Corporate Information 2 Built to Endure. Ready to Grow 4 Economic and Industry analysis 6 Short analysis about company’s positioning 8 Incredible at a glance 10 Statement from Chairman's Office 14 Our Manufacturing Excellence 16 Our Diversified Product Portfolio 18 Operational Excellence 20 Building a Trusted Steel Brand 22 Financial Highlights for FY2025-26 24 People & Communities 26 Environmental Stewardship 28 Governance in Action 30 Board of Directors Corporate Overview 31 Report of the Board of Director’s 45 Annexure A – Particulars of Energy Conservation, Technology Absorption and Foreign Exchange Earnings and Outgo as required under the Companies (Accounts) Rules, 2014: 47 Annexure B – Report on Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) Activities / Initiatives 50 Annexure C – Disclosure In Directors’ Report Pursuant To Section 197(12) of The Companies Act, 2013 Read With Rule 5(1) of The Companies (Appointment and Remuneration of Managerial Personnel) Amended Rules, 2016: 53 Annexure D – Secretarial Audit Report 57 Annexure E – Form No. AOC-2 58 Management Discussion and Analysis Report 68 Report on Corporate Governance Statutory Reports 101 Independent Auditor’s Report 112 Balance Sheet 113 Statement of Profit and Loss 114 Statement of Changes in Equity 115 Cash Flow Statement 117 Notes to the Financial Statements Financial Reports BOARD OF DIRECTORS Mr. Rama Shankar Gupta Executive Director-Chairman & Managing Director Mr. Sanjay Kaloya Non-Executive, Non-Independent Director Mr. Raj Prakash Verma Non-Executive, Non-Independent Director Mr. Deepak Kumar Agarwalla Non-Executive, Independent Director Mrs. Sonam Agarwal Non-Executive, Independent Director Mrs. Shilpi Modi Non-Executive, Independent Director CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER Shri Amit Agrawal COMPANY SECRETARY Shri Bharat Agarwal STATUTORY AUDITORS M/s. R. Gopal & Associates Chartered Accountants COST AUDITORS M/s. Dipak Lal & Associates Cost Accountants SECRETARIAL AUDITORS M/s. MR & Associates Company Secretaries INTERNAL AUDITORS M/s. G. P . Agarwal & Co. Chartered Accountants Corporate Information LENDERS Bank of India Central Bank of India Punjab National Bank Canara Bank REGISTERED OFFICE 14, Netaji Subhas Road 2nd Floor, Kolkata700 001 Phone/Fax: 033-2243 4355 / 2242-8551 CORPORATE OFFICE Lansdowne Towers 2/1 A, Sarat Bose Road, Kolkata-700 020 Phone: (033) 6638-4700 Fax: (033) 2289-0285 E-mailinvestorsiil@iilgroup.co.in Website: www.incredibleindustries.co.in WORKS Raturia, Angadpur Durgapur-713 215 Phone: (0343) 2591105 / 2591122 / 1123 / 1124 REGISTRAR & SHARE TRANSFER AGENT M/s. Maheshwari Datamatics Pvt. Ltd. 23, R. N. Mukherjee Road, 5th Floor Kolkata-700 001 Phone: (033) 2243-5809/5029 Fax: (033) 2248-4787 E-mailmdpldc@yahoo.com Like steel itself, every lasting enterprise begins as potential. It is refined through discipline, tempered by experience and defined by the choices made when no one is watching. Strength is not found in a single moment; it is built, layer upon layer, through consistency that never wavers. At Incredible Industries, this philosophy runs through everything we create. From billets that become new possibilities to bars that reinforce skylines, from wire rods that connect industries to nails that hold ideas together, every product is part of something larger than itself. Individually, they are products. BUIL T TO ENDURE ENDURANCE IS NEVER AN ACCIDENT. IT IS FORGED THROUGH PRESSURE, SHAPED BY PURPOSE AND STRENGTHENED WITH TIME. Together, they become the unseen framework of progress. The future is not built by standing still. It belongs to those who continue to evolve, while remaining true to their foundations. Growthis not merely the pursuit of scale, it is the quiet confidence to prepare before opportunity arrives, to strengthen before demand emerges and to invest in capabilities that will endure long after the next cycle has passed.As cities expand, industries evolve and infrastructure reshapes the nation, the need for dependable steel continues to grow. Meeting those future demands more than capacity, it demands consistency, precision and the ability to deliver with unwavering reliability. This is the future we are preparing for. By strengthening our manufacturing capabilities, embracing operational excellence and building on an integrated production ecosystem, we are creating an enterprise that is agile enough to seize opportunity and resilient enough to sustain it. READY TO GROW. Because growth is not simply about becoming bigger. It is about becoming ready for everything, the future chooses to build. The next decade belongs to nations that can build at scale and India's steel industry is preparing to lead that journey. Steel is the skeleton on which nations build ambition. In India, that ambition is accelerating. Contributing nearly 2% to GDP and backed by vast iron ore reserves and a formidable workforce, Currently, India is the second-largest crude steel producer in World. INCREDIBLE INDUSTRIES LIMITED | Annual Report 2025-26 4 Crude steel output rose from 151.14 MT in FY25 to 153.60 MT within the first eleven months of FY2025-26. India's demand for steel continues to gather momentum. With expanding infrastructure ambitions, rapid urban transformation connectivity investments, the nation is reshaping the way the infrastructure of tomorrow is conceived and constructed. As India moves towards 255 MT of crude steel production by 2030-31, every tonne forged brings the nation closer to a stronger and resilient industrial future. India continues to outperform with 3.9% year-on-year growth, strengthening its position as a globally competitive manufacturing and export hub. Corporate OverviewStatutory ReportFinancial Section INCREDIBLE INDUSTRIES LIMITED | Annual Report 2025-26 5",
