    "c30619d10327220eee0e3e1098a0dde750bd876f": {
      "url": "https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/IRCON_25082026232751_STXINTIMATION.pdf",
      "text": "IRCON/SECY/STEX/124 Dated: 25 th August, 2026 Sub: Disclosure under Regulation 30 of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015Imposition of fine by NSE & BSE for the quarter ended 30 th June, 2026. Dear Sir/ Madam, महोदय/ महोदया, Pursuant to Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 [“SEBI (LODR)”], it is to inform that National Stock Exchange of India Limited (“NSE”) and BSE Limited (“BSE”) vide their letter/ email dated 25 th August, 2026 have levied fine of Rs. 9,66,420/- each (incl. GST) on the Company for the non-compliance with Regulation 17(1), 18(1) and 19(1)/19(2) i.e. noncompliance for the composition of the Board and its committees for the quarter ended 30 th June, 2026. The Company, vide its letter dated 25 th August, 2026, has clarified to NSE and BSE that Ircon International Limited (“IRCON”) is a Government Company as per provisions of Section 2(45) of the Companies Act, 2013. As per provisions of the Companies Act, 2013 and Articles of Association of the Company, the President of India vests with the power to appoint Directors (including Independent Directors/Woman Director) on the Board of IRCON. All Directors in IRCON are appointed by the Government of India through its Administrative Ministry, Ministry of Railways (MoR) and IRCON has no role to play in the appointment of any Director including Independent Directors/Woman Director unless nominated by the Government of India. IRCON has been continuously requesting MoR for the appointment of requisite number of Independent Directors (including Woman Independent Director) on the Board of IRCON in order to ensure all compliances pertaining to Composition of the Board and its Committees. The fine imposed on the Company has no impact on the financial, operation or other activities of the Company. However, the same are being identified under “contingent liability” in the financial statements of the Company. This is to further inform that pursuant to MoR order dated 13 th August, 2026, One Woman Independent Director has been appointed on the Board of IRCON w.e.f.17 th August, 2026 and subsequently AC and NRC of the Company have been properly re-constituted w.e.f. 17 th August, 2026, as per applicable provisions and accordingly, the Company is eligible for the waiver of fines as per the SEBI’s policy for exemption of fines. It may be noted that in earlier instances of non-compliance, NSE & BSE had already waived off fine imposed on the Company upon attaining the requisite compliances. क ृ पया उपरोƅ जानकारी को įरकॉडŊ पर लŐ। Thankyou/धɊवाद, Yours faithfully/भवदीया, (Ůितभा अŤवाल)/ (Pratibha Aggarwal) क ं पनी सिचव एवं अनुपालन अिधकारी/ Company Secretary & Compliance Officer सद˟ता Ţ./ Membership No.: F8874 Date and time of event: 25th August, 2026 at 1907 Hrs. BSE Limited Listing Dept./ Dept. of Corporate Services Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai – 400001 बीएसई िलिमटेड िलİːंग िवभाग / कॉपŖरेट सेवा िवभाग पी. जे. टावसŊ, दलाल ː Ōीट, मुंबई– 400001 Scrip code / ID: 541956 / IRCON National Stock Exchange of India Limited Listing Department, Exchange Plaza, Plot no. C-1, G Block, Bandra –Kurla Complex, Bandra (East), Mumbai – 400051 नेशनल ːॉक एƛचŐज ऑफ इंिडया िलिमटेड िलİːंग िवभाग एƛचŐज ɘाजा, ɘॉट नं सी-1, जी ɰॉक, बांūा-क ु लाŊ कॉ̱ɘेƛ, बांūा (पूवŊ), मुंबई-400051 Scrip Code: IRCON",
