 taken, initiated or order(s) passed. Imposition of fine of Rs. 1,65,200 under Reg. 17(1) (basic fine Rs. 1,40,000 plus 18% GST Rs. 25,200) levied under SEBI SOP Circular provisions, by BSE and NSE separately; Imposition of fine of Rs. 1,36,880 under Reg. 17(1A) (basic fine Rs. 1,16,000 plus 18% GST Rs. 20,880) levied under SEBI SOP Circular provisions, by BSE and NSE separately; Total fine (incl 18% GST): Rs. 3,02,080 by BSE and NSE separately 3 Date of receipt of direction or order, including any ad - interim or interim orders, or any other communication from the authority. August 25, 2026 4 Details of the violation(s)/ contravention(s) committed or alleged to be committed. Non - compliance /delayed compliance with Regulations 17(1) and 17(1A) of the SEBI (LODR) Regulations pertaining to composition of the Board and appointment /continuation of non - executive Director who has attained the age of 75 years. 5 Impact on financial, operation or other activities of the listed entity, quantifiable in There is no material impact on the financial, operational or other activities of the Company, except for the payment of fine of Rs. 3,02,080/ - monetary terms to the extent possible. each by BSE and NSE, which has been duly paid . 6 Current status/explanation The underlying compliance under Regulation 17(1A) has already been complied with and made good on May 29, 2026. The fine has arisen as part of routine quarter - end SOP review process for the quarter ended June 30, 2026. The underlying compliance with respect to Board composition under Regulation 17(1) was made good on July 15, 2026.",
