      "text": "August 26, 2026 The Manager The Department of Corporate Services BSE Limited P. J. Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai - 400 001 Scrip Code – 540775 The Manager The Listing Department National Stock Exchange of India Limited Exchange Plaza, Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra (East), Mumbai - 400 051 Symbol - KHADIM Dear Sir / Madam, Sub: Disclosure under Regulation 30 read with Para B of Part A of Schedule III of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 read with SEBI Master Circular HO/49/14/14(7)2025-CFD-POD2/I/3762/2026 dated January 30, 2026 This is in continuation of our disclosure dated May 13, 2026 (enclosed herewith as Annexure “I”) in the matter of withholding of receivables by the Company and forfeiture of Performance Bank Guarantee, by Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan Authority (‘SSAA’), Punjab through Director General School Education-cumState Project Director (DG-School) (“the Tenderer”) in respect of a tender for supply of school shoes and uniform, floated by it. In accordance with the order of the Hon’ble High Court of Punjab and Haryana, Chandigarh, dated May 05, 2026, the Company has received the outstanding amount of ₹ 31,96,86,729/- (Rupees Thirty One Crores Ninety Six Lakhs Eighty Six Thousand Seven Hundred and Twenty Nine) along with the applicable interest and other related dues from the concerned party. We request you to take the same on record. Thanking You, Yours faithfully, For Khadim India Limited Group Company Secretary & Head – Legal ICSI Membership No.: A21358 Encl: As above May 13, 2026 The Manager The Department of Corporate Services BSE Limited P. J. Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai - 400 001 Scrip Code – 540775 The Manager The Listing Department National Stock Exchange of India Limited Exchange Plaza, Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra (East), Mumbai - 400 051 Symbol - KHADIM Dear Sir / Madam, Sub: Disclosure under Regulation 30 read with Para B of Part A of Schedule III of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 read with SEBI Master Circular HO/49/14/14(7)2025-CFD-POD2/I/3762/2026 issued on July 11, 2023 (last updated on January 30, 2026) This is in continuation of our disclosure dated August 11, 2023 (enclosed herewith as Annexure “A”) and October 31, 2023 (enclosed herewith as Annexure “B”) in the matter of withholding of receivables by the Company and forfeiture of Performance Bank Guarantee, by Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan Authority (SSAA), Punjab through Director General School Education -cum-State Project Director (DG -School) (“the Tenderer”) in respect of a tender for supply of school shoes and uniform, floated by it. Kindly note that in the said matter, the Hon’ble High Court of Punjab and Haryana, Chandigarh vide its order dated May 05, 2026 (Order copy received by us on May 12, 2026) has confirmed the Arbitral Award passed on June 27, 2022 which was in favour of the Company and rejected the order dated August 16, 2023 passed by the Learned District Court at Mohali, in favour of the Tenderer. We request you to take the same on record. Thanking You, Yours faithfully, For Khadim India Limited Group Company Secretary & Head – Legal ICSI Membership No.: A21358 Encl: As above ABHIJIT DAN Digitally signed by ABHIJIT DAN Date: 2026.05.13 16:41:07 +05'30' Annexure-I Annexure\"A\" October 31, 2023 The Manager The Department of Corporate Services BSE Limited P. J. Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai - 400 001 Scrip Code – 540775 The Manager The Listing Department National Stock Exchange of India Limited Exchange Plaza, Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra (East), Mumbai - 400 051 Symbol - KHADIM Dear Sir / Madam, Sub: Disclosure under Regulation 30 of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 This is in continuation of our disclosure dated August 11, 2023 made under Regulation 30 read with Para B of Part A of Schedule III of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 vide its Notification No. SEBI/LAD -NRO/GN/2023/131 dated June 14, 2023 and SEBI Circular No. SEBI/HO/CFD/CFD-PoD-1/P/CIR/2023/123 dated July 13, 2023. Kindly note that in the matter of “Appeal against Arbitral Award dated June 27, 2022”, the Learned District Court at Mohali vide its order dated August 16, 2023 has decided in favour of Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan Authority (SSAA), Punjab and Director General School Education -cum-State Project Director (DG - School) (“the Tenderer”) and set aside the Arbitral Award. Being aggrieved by the order, the Company has filed its ap peal before the Hon’ble High Court of Punjab, Chandigarh , today, i.e., on October 31, 2023. We request you to take the same on record. Thanking You, Yours faithfully, For Khadim India Limited Company Secretary & Head – Legal ICSI Membership No.: A21358 ABHIJIT DAN Digitally signed by ABHIJIT DAN Date: 2023.10.31 15:52:38 +05'30' Annexure \"B\"",
